  "text": "No ancient people called themselves the Celts. They used tribal names such as Belgae, Cantii, Brigantes, and Arverni. A name could come from an ancestor, a god, a totem animal, or a holy place. The term Celt might have begun as one such name. It became a generic term other Europeans used for the whole people. There is no agreed definition of Celtic society or worldview. Some argue that Celts absorbed earlier local cultures wherever they settled. A narrow definition holds that a Celt is someone who spoke a Celtic language.",
